A||N||28||Haze_Performance||17" Fiero Wheels||||12||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-25-2000||02:04 AM||||I would like to put on a set of 17" wheels (For Shows) How large can I go without rubbing the tires?? P.S I have a set of Ebach Lowering Springs on the car.(its a 85 2M4)<P>Wheel Size?<P>Tire Size?<P>Offset?<P>If 17" will be a problem how about the same info with a 16" ??<P><BR>Thank You<BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||12
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||07-25-2000||05:34 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mm_sfera_a.jpg"> <P>How about these?? Heres the info:<P>Wheels:<BR>   Mille Miglia Sfera<BR>Finish:<BR>   Silver w/Machined Lip<BR>Size:<BR>   16x7.5 (That sounds a little big?)<BR>Price:<BR>   $155ea<BR>Availability:<BR>   In Stock<BR>TireSize:<BR>   205/55-16  <P>The above wheels are from tirerack.com, They say they fit a Fiero. But I thought that I would ask a fellow Fiero owner first...<P><BR>T/Y<BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||4
Z||000002||1FST2M6||07-25-2000||08:12 AM||||i had 17x7.5 (42mm offset) in the front with 215-40 and on the rear i had a 245-40 on a 17x8 (45mm offset) You'll be HARD PRESSED to break those loose... my car on nitrous would roast them but not for long.. MAYBE 20ft! and toss it into ANY corner and you'll be plastered to the window before she slides. Thats what I found... I was using Yokohama A520s. Had Eibachs and Konis.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis1_3.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||07-25-2000||08:40 AM||||You could try Compomotive three piece wheels.They are very nice but also very expensive. I was quoted ~$2000 total for one pair of 17x8 and one pair of 17x10 in their CXN style: <A HREF="http://www.usacomp.com/cxn.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.usacomp.com/cxn.htm</A> <P>It looks a lot like the stock mesh wheels, too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||07-25-2000||10:12 AM||||I've decided on ASA JS5's in 17x7.5 and the Tire Rack recommended 215/45-sr17's.  I reccomend anything at least S-rated.  Check out the ASA's, they compliment the notchback design great!<P>PS-they're only about $600 for the set of 4!! (minus tires)<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car<p>[This message has been edited by b lo 0 (edited 07-25-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||Philphine||07-25-2000||10:14 AM||||16x7.5 panther 106's (35mm offset) with 225/50-16's in front and 255/50-16's in rear (coilovers needed). more tire than i need i know but i like the look. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||07-25-2000||11:34 AM||||DON'T skimp on the tires! Go with a Dunlop W10, Dunlop SP8000, Yoko A520, Yoko AVS inter., Nitto NT555, or BFG T/A KD.  if you get a hard compound tire with a tiny sidewall (45%) you'll easily find the limit of adhesion of the tire and your nice shiney wheels will be toast...  spend the extra $20-30 per tire and get somthing you'll like. I'd stay away from Toyo FZ4, the Nitto NT450. You might want to ask about the Kumho ECSTR Supra 712. Stick tire, proper size and great price. also available at the tire rack. might also want to check out <A HREF="http://www.tires.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tires.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.washingtontire.com" TARGET=_blank>www.washingtontire.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||07-25-2000||12:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>i had 17x7.5 (42mm offset) in the front with 215-40 and on the rear i had a 245-40 on a 17x8 (45mm offset) You'll be HARD PRESSED to break those loose... my car on nitrous would roast them but not for long.. MAYBE 20ft! and toss it into ANY corner and you'll be plastered to the window before she slides. Thats what I found... I was using Yokohama A520s. Had Eibachs and Konis.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis1_3.jpg">  <P>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-25-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So i shouldnt have any problem with just bolting 16" x 7.5" on , all around huh??<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||14
Z||000008||1FST2M6||07-25-2000||01:37 PM||||NOPE no problem at all.. with a 7 or 7.5 inch wide wheel you can run a 42mm offset with an 8" wide wheel a 45 mm offset is nesessary. But just dont skimp on tires...  ||||reg||1
