Z||000017||1FST2M6||07-26-2000||08:16 AM||||48mm offset! why so much? 17x9 ? a good tire for the stock 14s is the Yokohama A509 (out of production) or the Yokohama AVS imtermediate. <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>    16"s will fit fine you don't need coil overs for ANY of the mentioned wheel sets. You'll just have a car with nicer wheels that looks 4wd. with out any lowering spring/system. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||fieroshop||07-26-2000||10:31 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gt1_4.jpg"> <BR>I have 215/45/17 in front and 235/45/17 in the rear. My GT is also lowered and I do not rub anywhere. The difference in actual size between the stock wheel and the 17's I'm using is .07" in the front and .17" in the rear. Using these sizes I did not have to worry about whether the speedo needed to be recalculated<P>------------------<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000019||b lo 0||07-26-2000||10:41 AM||||86_fastback-good job on picking ASA's.<P>And Hypnotise, I hope you didn't pay too much for those Konigs, my 17x7.5 ASA JS5's look exactly like them and were only about $600 a set.  Often times, if you buy Konigs or Players or other easily recognizeable brand name show wheels, you're paying for the name  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  However, those Konigs do make your fastback look kinda Ferrari-esque, huh?  <P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">  <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||4
Z||000020||86_Fastback||07-26-2000||10:57 AM||||Actually, my wheels and tires were from an ebay auction.  With 3000 miles, it cost me $610.<P>The wheels are 17X7.5   The 48mm offset is only 13mm more than stock(35mm).  Since the wheels are  0.5"  (12.7mm) wider, the extra width is put in the fenders and will not stick out any further than stock.||||reg||1
